A||||3||Gokart||Valve cover wouldn't come off!||||8||
Z||000000||Gokart||12-30-1999||10:08 PM||||Just changed the valve cover gasket in the wifes mini-van last weekend and it took 20 minutes. Then started on mine and it took me two hours to try to get it off then give up and put it back on!! I removed all the screws and the engine mount thats in the way, but there seems to be two metal protruding objects under the cover that keeps it from sliding down and out! Is there a way to get it out without having to remove the plenum and manifolds?||||reg||8
Z||000001||cobra427||12-31-1999||04:03 AM||||Hi, it shows in the factory service manual a discription of the procedure on removing both the front and rear rocker covers and also a pic at the end of the procedure with the plenum off.I have heard it said that after you get the covers off, you can alter the insides enough to be able to take them off the next time without having to take off the plenum. Don't know for sure on that as I have never had to remove them as yet.<BR>did you get your timing straightened out yet?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Linx||12-31-1999||04:05 AM||||Must you remove the plenum?  v6?  Yup.  Cant <I>slide</I> it out because the valves are in the way.  Don't fret about the work, tho'; after you've done it a few times, you can whip them intake manifolds off in an hour.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Linx (edited 12-31-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Gokart||12-31-1999||06:02 AM||||Thanks guys! My factory service manual won't get here soon enough for me and when it does I'm going to burn my Haynes manual!! Cobra427, read my other post on Tech. Disc. posted yesterday about my timing under "used distributor". I got hosed!||||reg||14
